From 1de556cdd007102995478d0911cf93134b9509ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 14:35:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] MFront: fixes of the generic-parallel interface for material
 properties

- stlpar backend: the points are traversed by a counting iterator. With
  libstdc++, the parallel algorithms ran sequentially on the iterators of
  std::views::iota, whose C++17 category is not random access. The
  iterator is shared with the generic-parallel interface for behaviours.
- Errors: errno is no longer checked after the parallel execution. It is
  thread-local, does not exist on GPUs and is modified by the runtimes
  (for instance at the initialisation of TBB or CUDA, which made the first
  call fail). The kernels now report invalid results (nan, infinite) in
  the array of statuses (status -4, as documented).
- The bounds of the output were written past the end of the array of
  statuses and never analysed.
- Headers of the backends installed in their sub-directories: they were
  installed in MFront/, where the AbstractBackend.hxx files of the two
  interfaces overwrote each other.
---
 mfront/include/CMakeLists.txt                 |  8 +--
 .../MaterialProperty/BackendBase.hxx          | 31 ++++----
 .../GenericParallelBehaviour/ParallelSTL.hxx  | 72 ++-----------------
 .../MaterialProperty/BackendBase.cxx          | 14 ++--
 .../MaterialProperty/CUDABackendBase.cxx      |  8 +--
 .../CxxProgrammingModelBackendBase.cxx        |  6 +-
 6 files changed, 41 insertions(+), 98 deletions(-)

